CONTEXT SHIFT / STALE BRIDGE
A subset of previously valid phase-0 bridges
is:
semantically invalid
in later phases.

A retain-all policy
continues:
paying memory cost

and:
can also pay:
wrong-interface consequence
when:
stale shortcuts remain active.

Selective policies use:
current fit
to:
remove:
execution authority.

Important distinction:

BRIDGE MEMORY

and

CURRENT BRIDGE AUTHORITY

are:
separate state.

A stale bridge may be:
stored
for:
future recurrence

without:
being:
currently executable.

RECURRENCE VALUE
